1. **The Irreducible $\epsilon$-Hallucination Bound:**
   An autoregressive transformer computes conditional token probabilities:
   $$P(w_1, w_2, \dots, w_T) = \prod_{t=1}^T P(w_t \mid w_1, \dots, w_{t-1})$$
   Because it is inherently probabilistic, its probability of an omission or error is strictly non-zero ($\epsilon > 0$). In consumer chatbots, a 99.9% accuracy rate is considered state-of-the-art. In clinical triage, **a 0.1% failure rate means 1 out of every 1,000 emergency cardiac patients or lethal drug interactions (e.g. Warfarin + Yograj Guggulu or Furosemide + Yashtimadhu) will be missed.** In medical jurisprudence and ethics, $\epsilon > 0$ on life-safety invariants is unacceptable.

2. **The Kiosk Hardware Latency Collapse:**
   A standard 8B LLM running locally on edge kiosk hardware (Intel Core i5 / RK3588 / Celeron with 8GB RAM) executes at **2 to 5 tokens per second**. Transcribing and parsing a 300-word patient dialogue takes **60 to 90 seconds**. 
   In an Indian government OPD (e.g., AIIA New Delhi or AIIMS) where 5,000 patients arrive between 8:00 AM and 11:00 AM, a 60-second processing time collapses the entire hospital lobby within 20 minutes. Our deterministic and hybrid kernel parses the clinical state in **0.039 milliseconds** ($>27,000\text{ cases/sec}$).

3. **Statutory Air-Gap Law (DPDP Act 2023 & DISHA):**
   Commercial cloud APIs (OpenAI GPT-4o, Anthropic Claude 3.5, Google Gemini Cloud) transmit unredacted audio and clinical transcripts across public networks to remote data centers. For national healthcare infrastructure under the **Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023**, **DISHA**, and the **Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM)**, transmitting citizen health records across uncertified external cloud boundaries is prohibited. The system must operate 100% air-gapped on bare-metal hardware ($0.00\text{ Mbps}$ internet).

